---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import { withBase, sourceUrl } from '../../lib/paths';
import scope from '../../../catalog/frontend-scope.json';
const paths = [
  { n:'01', title:'Give state one owner.', detail:'Navigation in the URL. Remote records in the query cache. Unsaved values in the form. Derived values are not another store.', id:'react-state-ownership', label:'React State Ownership' },
  { n:'02', title:'Make failure a real state.', detail:'Keep useful same-identity data when refresh fails. Restore an owned optimistic update without erasing a newer result.', id:'tanstack-query-engineering', label:'TanStack Query Engineering' },
  { n:'03', title:'Make the action understandable.', detail:'A coherent icon family, a named button, visible focus and a responsive layout. The glyph supports meaning; it does not replace it.', id:'icon-system-integration', label:'Icon System Integration' },
];
const cases = [
  { title:'A background refresh fails', expected:'Keep the same workspace’s previously accepted rows, show a refresh error and retain a reachable retry action.', source:'frontend-loading-error-states' },
  { title:'The server rejects a form', expected:'Keep the draft, map the error to its field and focus a useful control. Reset only after an accepted save.', source:'react-forms-validation' },
  { title:'An old search finishes late', expected:'The new filter owns the view. Query identity and cancellation prevent the obsolete result from replacing it.', source:'tanstack-query-engineering' },
  { title:'A narrow screen hides an action', expected:'Adapt the layout while preserving required controls and reading order. Do not hide the entire document’s overflow to conceal a defect.', source:'responsive-ui-implementation' },
];
const snippet = `import { BsArrowClockwise } from 'react-icons/bs';\n\n<button type="button" aria-label="Refresh items" onClick={refresh}>\n  <BsArrowClockwise aria-hidden="true" focusable="false" />\n</button>`;
---
<Base title="Frontend Engineering — Worked Guide" active="bundles" description="Original React, query, form, Tailwind and icon procedures with an isolated executable fixture and clear evidence boundaries.">
<div class="container frontend-guide">
  <a class="back-link" href={withBase('categories/frontend-engineering/')}>← Frontend Engineering</a>
  <header class="guide-hero"><p class="eyebrow">{scope.skills.length} ORIGINAL SKILLS · THREE FOCUSED BUNDLES</p><h1>Interfaces that<br/><span>hold together.</span></h1><p class="guide-intro">React architecture, deliberate data flow and a coherent design system. Build the happy path—and the states that make an interface dependable.</p>
    <div class="stack-list" aria-label="Topics"><span>React</span><span>Next.js</span><span>TanStack Query</span><span>Tailwind</span><span>React Hook Form</span><span>React Icons</span></div>
    <div class="guide-actions"><a class="button primary" href={withBase('bundles/modern-react/')}>Explore Modern React →</a><a class="button secondary" href={sourceUrl('evals/frontend/README.md')}>Run the isolated React fixture ↗</a></div>
  </header>
  <section class="guide-section" aria-labelledby="decisions"><div class="section-label"><p class="eyebrow">START WITH OWNERSHIP</p><h2 id="decisions">Three decisions before more code.</h2></div>
    <div class="decision-grid">{paths.map(p=><article class="decision-card"><span class="step-number">{p.n}</span><h3>{p.title}</h3><p>{p.detail}</p><a href={withBase(`skills/${p.id}/`)}>{p.label} →</a></article>)}</div>
  </section>
  <section class="guide-split guide-section" aria-labelledby="icon-title"><article><p class="eyebrow">DESIGN MEETS BEHAVIOR</p><h2 id="icon-title">An icon is not<br/>an accessible name.</h2><p>Use the existing family, import deliberately and name the action on the button. Keep the SVG decorative when the control already carries its meaning.</p><p class="fine-print">React Icons and its source icon families remain external libraries. The fixture preserves their notices; the original skill is the integration procedure.</p><a class="text-link" href={withBase('skills/icon-system-integration/')}>Read the icon integration skill →</a></article><div class="code-panel"><div class="code-caption">Original React recipe / Bootstrap family</div><pre><code>{snippet}</code></pre><p>Named imports · Keyboard semantics · Decorative SVG · Family notices</p></div></section>
  <section class="guide-section" aria-labelledby="states"><div class="section-label"><p class="eyebrow">BEYOND THE HAPPY PATH</p><h2 id="states">A state matrix you can inspect.</h2></div><div class="state-list">{cases.map(c=><details><summary>{c.title}</summary><div><p>{c.expected}</p><a href={withBase(`skills/${c.source}/`)}>Open the responsible skill →</a></div></details>)}</div></section>
  <section class="guide-section evidence-card" aria-labelledby="fixture"><div><p class="eyebrow">EXECUTABLE SOURCE, SEPARATE FROM THE GUIDE</p><h2 id="fixture">A small React fixture.<br/>A clear testing boundary.</h2><p>The optional local example actually uses React, TanStack Query, React Hook Form, Tailwind and React Icons. Its test-controlled API uses synthetic data. This public guide is static—it does not run that app or connect to a product.</p></div><div><strong>Inspect, install deliberately, then qualify.</strong><pre><code>npm ci --prefix evals/frontend --ignore-scripts{`\n`}npm --prefix evals/frontend run check{`\n`}npm --prefix evals/frontend run build{`\n`}npm --prefix evals/frontend test</code></pre><a href={sourceUrl('docs/FRONTEND_ENGINEERING.md')}>Coverage, browser commands and limits ↗</a><p class="fine-print">Not a Next.js deployment, live-agent evaluation, screen-reader certification or field performance result.</p></div></section>
  <nav class="bundle-next" aria-label="Frontend bundles"><a href={withBase('bundles/modern-react/')}><span>BUILD</span><strong>Modern React Applications →</strong></a><a href={withBase('bundles/frontend-performance/')}><span>MEASURE</span><strong>Frontend Performance and Reliability →</strong></a><a href={withBase('bundles/interface-design/')}><span>DESIGN</span><strong>Interface Design Systems →</strong></a></nav>
</div>
</Base>
<style>
.eyebrow { font:11px/1.7 var(--font-mono,monospace); letter-spacing:.13em; color:var(--muted); }
:global(html[data-theme=light]) .guide-hero h1 span, :global(html[data-theme=light]) .step-number, :global(html[data-theme=light]) .decision-card a, :global(html[data-theme=light]) .state-list a, :global(html[data-theme=light]) .evidence-card a { color:#477731; }
.frontend-guide { padding-top:44px; padding-bottom:80px; }
.guide-hero { padding:52px 0 62px; max-width:870px; }
.guide-hero h1 { font-size:clamp(46px,6.2vw,82px); line-height:1.04; letter-spacing:-.055em; margin:22px 0; }
.guide-hero h1 span { color:var(--accent); }
.guide-intro { max-width:660px; font-size:19px; line-height:1.65; color:var(--muted); }
.stack-list,.guide-actions { display:flex; flex-wrap:wrap; gap:10px; margin-top:26px; }
.stack-list span { border:1px solid var(--line); border-radius:7px; padding:7px 10px; color:var(--muted); font-size:12px; }
.guide-actions { gap:14px; margin-top:28px; }
.guide-section { border-top:1px solid var(--line); padding:42px 0; }
.section-label h2,.guide-split h2,.evidence-card h2 { font-size:clamp(26px,3.2vw,37px); line-height:1.16; letter-spacing:-.035em; margin:12px 0 24px; }
.decision-grid { display:grid; grid-template-columns:repeat(3,minmax(0,1fr)); gap:18px; }
.decision-card { border:1px solid var(--line); background:var(--surface); border-radius:14px; padding:25px; display:flex; flex-direction:column; }
.step-number { font:12px var(--font-mono,monospace); color:var(--accent); }
.decision-card h3 { font-size:21px; letter-spacing:-.025em; line-height:1.25; margin:28px 0 12px; }
.decision-card p,.guide-split p,.evidence-card p { color:var(--muted); line-height:1.7; }
.decision-card a { margin-top:auto; padding-top:18px; font-size:12px; color:var(--accent); }
.guide-split { display:grid; grid-template-columns:minmax(0,.85fr) minmax(0,1.15fr); align-items:center; gap:44px; }
.code-panel { border:1px solid var(--line); border-radius:14px; min-width:0; background:var(--surface); }
.code-caption { padding:16px 21px; border-bottom:1px solid var(--line); font-size:12px; color:var(--muted); }
.code-panel pre,.evidence-card pre { padding:22px; margin:0; max-width:100%; white-space:pre-wrap; overflow-wrap:anywhere; font:12px/1.85 var(--font-mono,monospace); }
.code-panel p { font-size:11px; border-top:1px solid var(--line); padding:14px 21px; margin:0; }
.fine-print { font-size:12px; line-height:1.7; }
.state-list { border:1px solid var(--line); border-radius:12px; overflow:hidden; }
.state-list details+details { border-top:1px solid var(--line); }
.state-list summary { padding:21px 24px; cursor:pointer; font-weight:600; }
.state-list summary:focus-visible { outline:2px solid var(--accent); outline-offset:-4px; }
.state-list details>div { padding:0 24px 24px; max-width:860px; line-height:1.7; color:var(--muted); }
.state-list a { font-size:13px; color:var(--accent); }
.evidence-card { display:grid; grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr; gap:42px; }
.evidence-card pre { margin:16px 0; padding:16px; background:var(--surface); border:1px solid var(--line); border-radius:9px; }
.evidence-card strong { font-size:14px; }
.evidence-card a { font-size:13px; color:var(--accent); }
.bundle-next { display:grid; grid-template-columns:repeat(3,minmax(0,1fr)); gap:16px; }
.bundle-next a { padding:20px; border:1px solid var(--line); border-radius:12px; }
.bundle-next span { display:block; color:var(--muted); font-size:10px; letter-spacing:.12em; margin-bottom:13px; }
.bundle-next strong { font-size:15px; line-height:1.5; }
@media(max-width:800px) { .decision-grid,.guide-split,.evidence-card,.bundle-next { grid-template-columns:1fr; } .guide-hero { padding:35px 0 42px; } .guide-section { padding:32px 0; } .guide-split,.evidence-card { gap:24px; } .decision-card h3 { margin-top:20px; } }
</style>
